/// The transcript's module: answers, to `build`, the program's standard
/// output, the `Transcript` `platform transcript` is. Built on its first
/// demand, or by the loader when an image names it.
///
/// The factory pattern `PlatformFactory.ns` is written in: this root holds
/// the VM mirror, which the platform's root hands it, and nothing hands its
/// instance to a program. The platform's root builds it through the
/// mirror on its first use -- again after an unwind interrupted that use,
/// which records nothing -- and keeps it in a private lazy slot, and
/// each platform's `transcript` getter sends it `build`, its one public
/// member. Its nested classes are private and reach the mirror lexically,
/// as members of this root, never through a slot of their own. Nothing a
/// program can name answers this root's instance or its class, so no
/// program can build one over something that is not the mirror. Keep it
/// so: no code whose receiver is this root's instance may send it anything
/// it does not understand, since a `MessageNotUnderstood` hands its
/// receiver to whoever catches it.
///
/// The factory's parameter is copied into a slot because neither a lazy
/// slot nor a method may name it (§6). A send to `vmMirror` here is a
/// mirror send, as in `Kernel.ns`: this module is resolved with
/// `resolve_kernel`, which only shipped source is.
///
/// A value (§3.1.1): stateless but for the mirror the host hands it, so
/// every transcript is equal to every other.
///
/// @factory makes the transcript's module over `mirror`, copied into its
/// slot `vmMirror`. The platform's root sends it to the class the mirror
/// answers on the module's first demand, and again on the next demand
/// after an unwind interrupted one, which records nothing; the loader
/// sends it instead when an image names the module.
/// @param mirror the VM mirror, through which the transcript writes.
(* :module: newspeak.core.TranscriptFactory *)
class TranscriptFactory usingVmMirror: mirror = Value (
  |
    /// The VM mirror the factory was given: the one object through which
    /// the transcript writes. Never handed out.
    private vmMirror = mirror.
  |
) (
  /// The program's standard output: writes text, line breaks and the
  /// printed form of any object, as UTF-8, in the order they are sent.
  ///
  /// `show:` writes a string as it is and refuses anything else, as an
  /// ordinary error; `print:` writes any object's `printString`. The
  /// leaf never declines, so the failure blocks never run.
  private class Transcript = Value () (
    /// Writes `text` to standard output as it is, flushed at once.
    ///
    /// @param text a String or a Symbol.
    /// @answers the receiver.
    /// @signals ArgumentError carrying `text`, 'show: requires a String,
    /// got …', for any other argument; nothing is written.
    public show: text = (
      ^vmMirror transcript: self show: text ifFail: [nil].
    )

    /// Writes a line break to standard output, after everything written
    /// before it.
    ///
    /// @answers the receiver.
    public newLine = (
      ^vmMirror transcriptNewLine: self ifFail: [nil].
    )

    /// Writes the `printString` of `object` to standard output, as
    /// `show:` does.
    ///
    /// A method of its own rather than a `show:` that takes any object,
    /// since `show:` writes a String as it is and a String's `printString`
    /// quotes it: `print: 'text'` writes 'text', quotes included, where
    /// `show: 'text'` writes text.
    ///
    /// @param object any object; sent `printString`, whose answer must be
    /// a String or a Symbol, or `show:` signals its ArgumentError.
    /// @answers the receiver.
    /// @signals ArgumentError the one `show:` signals, carrying the answer
    /// of `printString`, when that answer is neither a String nor a Symbol.
    /// @signals Error every one `object`'s `printString` signals, before
    /// anything is written.
    /// @see `show:`.
    public print: object = (
      ^self show: object printString.
    )
  )

  /// Builds the program's standard output: the one public member of the
  /// module, named `build` like every shipped factory's.
  ///
  /// @answers a new `Transcript`, the program's standard output.
  public build = (
    ^Transcript new.
  )
)
